{{!--
  The crates part of THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt; notices/generate.sh writes the
  rest. It replaces each LOCK_SHA256(<name> <version>) with that crate's
  checksum from Cargo.lock, which cargo metadata does not carry, and each
  SOURCE_PATH(<path>) with a path that does not depend on this machine's cargo
  home. Triple braces throughout: the output is plain text, and double braces
  would escape it as HTML.
--}}
================================================================================
Rust crates
================================================================================

These {{len crates}} crates are compiled into at least one release target, or
into building one (build scripts and procedural macros), each under the licence
shown. The licence texts follow, each with the file it was taken from and the
crates it covers. A path that starts with <name>-<version>/ is in that crate's
package; any other is in the package, or the repository at the published
commit, of a crate listed under it. A text marked "standard text" is the
licence's SPDX text, used where a crate ships no copy of its own.

{{#each crates}}
  {{{package.name}}} {{{package.version}}}: {{{license}}}
{{/each}}
{{#each licenses}}

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{{{name}}} ({{{id}}}){{#unless source_path}}, standard text{{/unless}}
{{#unless source_path}}

The crates below ship no copy of this licence, so its standard text follows,
with a placeholder for the copyright line. Each is listed with the authors and
repository its Cargo.toml names.
{{/unless}}

{{#if source_path}}
Text from SOURCE_PATH({{{source_path}}}), used by:
{{else}}
Used by:
{{/if}}
{{#each used_by}}
  {{{crate.name}}} {{{crate.version}}}
{{#unless ../source_path}}
    authors:    {{#each crate.authors}}{{#unless @first}}, {{/unless}}{{{this}}}{{else}}none listed{{/each}}
    repository: {{{crate.repository}}}
{{/unless}}
{{/each}}
{{#if (eq id "MPL-2.0")}}

The binaries carry this crate unmodified. Its Source Code Form is the crate as
